WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.290
(soft music)

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.300
- [Host] Chinese President Xi Jinping met

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.250
with his Russian counterpart
during a state visit

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.153
to Moscow.

00:00:06.153 --> 00:00:09.390
(Vladimir speaking foreign language)

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.680
And is soon expected to talk

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.780
to Ukrainian president Volodymir Zelensky

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.689
for the first time since the war started.

00:00:14.689 --> 00:00:16.020
(camera clicking)

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.610
While the west has expressed concerns

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.770
over China's deepening ties with Russia,

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.050
Beijing has indicated an
ambition to help bring

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.510
about talks toward a ceasefire in Ukraine.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.660
- Xi jinping, one of his
main goals is to make China

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.950
get into a a superpower.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:30.932
And so part of that is being involved

00:00:30.932 --> 00:00:35.932
in security discussions and
peace talks around the world.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.550
- [Host] Recent diplomatic
breakthrough is brokered by China

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.010
offered tangible evidence
that Beijing is willing

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.790
to use its influence to help
resolve foreign disputes.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.770
Austin Ramsey covers China's global reach

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.260
for the Journal and explains
what Beijing's model

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.573
of a new diplomacy means for the US.

00:00:52.805 --> 00:00:54.750
(upbeat music)

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.358
On March 10th, Iran and
Saudi Arabia announced

00:00:57.358 --> 00:01:00.750
that they agreed to reestablish
diplomatic relations

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.430
after seven years of estrangement

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.514
in a deal mediated by China.

00:01:04.514 --> 00:01:08.764
(Wang speaking foreign language)

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.490
- This is a sort of thing
that would be difficult

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.080
for the US to bring about.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.840
The US doesn't have formal ties with Iran

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.460
and is of course very critical
of the Iranian authorities.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.420
There was obviously a concern
that the US had lost clout

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.650
particularly in the Middle East,

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:31.743
and China was now playing
this much more important role.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.770
- [Host] And this wasn't
the first showcase

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.663
of Xi's diplomatic ambitions.

00:01:37.665 --> 00:01:40.530
Last June, China offered to quote,

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.440
silence the guns across the
troubled horn of Africa,

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.260
at its first regional Peace conference.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.970
Delegates from six countries gathered

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.010
in Ethiopia to hear China's pledge

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.740
that Beijing was best
placed to restore stability

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.850
to the region.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.020
- The Chinese approach

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.750
to these negotiations
can be very different

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.250
from the United States.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.350
China has a policy of non-interference,

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:04.170
which often means not being critical

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.410
of governments and just focusing
on bringing them together.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:10.170
That can be very appealing,
especially to governments

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.420
that don't want their records examined.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.340
- [Host] While China
has sought to contrast

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.200
its regional policy with the US,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.760
Washington has accused Beijing

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.100
of using the mediation
dialogues to bolster

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.705
authoritarian regimes and
expand its security footprint.

00:02:23.705 --> 00:02:25.680
(bomb exploding)

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.260
An analyst say securing
any diplomatic wins

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.380
in Ukraine would be a much
tougher challenge for Beijing.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.840
European Capitals and
Washington have so far

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.960
greeted Beijing's diplomatic
push with skepticism.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.995
- China can't have it
both ways when it comes to

00:02:38.995 --> 00:02:42.360
the Russian aggression Ukraine,

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.420
it can't be putting
forward peace proposals

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.350
on the one hand while
actually feeding the flames

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.740
of the fire that Russia has
started, with the other hand.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:56.610
- Both Xi Jinping and Vladimir
Putin share a deep distrust

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.500
of the US and the West, and
they see the world order as led

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.620
by the West to the detriment
of their own countries

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.230
and so it's very harmful for China,

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:10.560
if Russia is damaged by
the war and it no longer

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.250
can play a role in supporting
this effort to sort

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.910
of lessen American and Western
influence over the world.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.770
- [Host] As part of its
push for what Xi calls

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:22.590
big power diplomacy,
Beijing increased its budget

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.640
for diplomatic travel

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.823
and other related
expenses by 12% this year.

00:03:27.847 --> 00:03:29.010
(soft music)

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.698
In a bid to counter China's inroads.

00:03:31.698 --> 00:03:33.457
- It's very, very good feedback in Africa.

00:03:33.457 --> 00:03:35.850
- [Host] Secretary of State,
Anthony Blinken traveled

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:39.315
to Ethiopia and Negele in
mid-March and he's just one

00:03:39.315 --> 00:03:42.030
of the many US officials
who are visiting regions

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.090
where Washington and Beijing
are competing for influence.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.910
- I think nothing focuses
the US like a competitor.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.470
This could sort of bring

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:52.890
about sort of renewed
American efforts to engage

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.380
in diplomacy around the
world, engage in diplomacy

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:58.350
in some places that the
US might have ignored,

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.944
a little bit in in recent years.

00:03:59.944 --> 00:04:02.444
(soft music)

